The \emph{connection matrix} \textcolor{black}{$\mathbf{M}$} of $(\Sigma;F,G)$ is an $m \times b$ matrix with all entries in $\{0,1,2\}$, determined by the following:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item if both vertices of bigon $B_j$ are glued to one pole $q_i$, then $\mathbf{M}_{ij}:=2$ ;
        \item if vertices of $B_j$ are glued to different poles $q_i\neq q_{i'}$, then $\mathbf{M}_{ij}=\mathbf{M}_{i'j}:=1$;
        \item all the other entries are $0$.
    \end{itemize}

For generic foliated surface $(\Sigma;F,G)$, 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mathrm{rank}(\mathbf{M}) \geq m-1$;
    \item the foliation pair $(F,G)$ is orientable if and only if $\mathrm{rank}(\mathbf{M}) = m-1$.
\end{enumerate}
